      "id": 197021809,
      "body": "I've been an owner since October ($10/share), so I'm glad to see you write this up!\n\nI think that discount from recent highs is a bit deceptive. AXIA underwent some sort of financial reorganization and spun out AXIA PRC to shareholders. The book value of the original AXIA shares is equal to the held AXIA shares plus the issued preferreds (based on the split ratio). So, I suspect that fall is a technical one, not a market drop, as my gains pre/post split remained the same (I think). My AXIA shares bvps revalued to $7.86 post split.\n\nI don't disagree with anything else you mention though! Looking forward to the deep dive.",
      "body_json": {
        "type": "doc",
        "attrs": {
          "schemaVersion": "v1"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I've been an owner since October ($10/share), so I'm glad to see you write this up!"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I think that discount from recent highs is a bit deceptive. AXIA underwent some sort of financial reorganization and spun out AXIA PRC to shareholders. The book value of the original AXIA shares is equal to the held AXIA shares plus the issued preferreds (based on the split ratio). So, I suspect that fall is a technical one, not a market drop, as my gains pre/post split remained the same (I think). My AXIA shares bvps revalued to $7.86 post split."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I don't disagree with anything else you mention though! Looking forward to the deep dive."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
